# AGENTS.md

## Project summary and core loop
LaunchPad is a 2D browser game. Create or load a captain, choose an unlocked mission, configure its rocket, crew, supplies and equipment within budget and lift limits, then launch from the pad. Manage turn-based mission resources and event decisions in Mission Control; successful missions unlock later operations.

Mission 2 (PUNCH) is one uncrewed launch carrying all four solar-observatory satellites, followed by staged deployment and commissioning. The game uses simplified, turn-based resource and event mechanics rather than real orbital or rigid-body physics.

## How to play / controls
Use the mouse to click Mission Control, select and plan a mission, then click the Launch Pad to review the launch checklist and begin. In Mission Control, click the flight-log screen to open the report; use its tabs and buttons to manage resources, answer events, continue phases or recall the mission. Menus and reports use mouse input. The space-center scene is a fixed 1280×800 logical canvas scaled to the viewport; it is not a walkable/isometric world.

## Important files
- `/index.html` — entry point, CSS, UI shell and module bootstrap
- `/main.js` — 2D Canvas space-center scene, pointer hotspots, resize/render loop and audio hooks
- `/ui.js` — captain/save flow, mission selection and planning, crew/resource simulation, Mission Control and report UI
- `/punch.js` — PUNCH four-satellite launch planner, deployment simulation and report visuals
- `/data.js` — missions, rockets, supplies, crew data and balance values
- `/artemis.js` — Artemis operations, event choices, history and lessons
- `/sprites.js` — sprite-sheet cropping, background removal, tinting and shared character rendering
- `/art_direction.md` — visual direction and typography guidance
- `/sound_direction.md` — audio direction
- `/rosebud/game-defaults.css`, `/rosebud/game-defaults.js` — platform-provided project helpers

